#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147162 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147482 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0e1c05a-7c23-59f5-a549-ec9a8d0415e6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Percentage"}] :question/id #uuid "034e763d-a3e1-52e8-90a7-9fac9ce11083" :question/math-academy-id "e-13108" :question/problem "What is $4 \\%$ of $35?$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part}=  \\textrm{percentage}\\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $35$, and the percentage is $4 \\%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n4 \\% = 4 \\div 100 = 0.04\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =4%\\times 35 \\\\  & =0.04\\times 35 \\\\  & =1.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4 \\%$ of $35$ is $1.4.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n4 \\% = \\dfrac{4}{100}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =4%\\times 35 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{100}\\times 35 \\\\  & =\\frac{140}{100} \\\\  & =1.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4 \\%$ of $35$ is $1.4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147163 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147483 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20feb2c2-bcec-5730-be40-da2f8e44be59" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Percentage Greater Than 100%"}] :question/id #uuid "a5fc07bc-6168-5525-acfb-a36ee021773d" :question/math-academy-id "e-13109" :question/problem "What is $140 \\%$ of $30?$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part}=  \\textrm{percentage}\\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $30$, and the percentage is $140\\%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n140 \\% = 140 \\div 100 = 1.4\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =140%\\times 30 \\\\  & =1.4\\times 30 \\\\  & =42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140 \\%$ of $30$ is $42.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n140 \\% = \\dfrac{140}{100} = \\dfrac{140 \\div 20}{100\\div 20} = \\dfrac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =140%\\times 30 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}\\times 30 \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{30}{5} \\\\  & =7\\times 6 \\\\  & =42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140 \\%$ of $30$ is $42.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147164 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0025f8a6-40fc-544b-abc7-e9c283da8f33" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Decimal Percentage"}] :question/id #uuid "8dde0f33-28c8-569b-a1f8-9390d8dafc35" :question/math-academy-id "e-13110" :question/problem "What is $3.6 \\%$ of $25?$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part}=  \\textrm{percentage}\\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $25$, and the percentage is $3.6 \\%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n3.6 \\% = 3.6 \\div 100 = 0.036\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =3.6%\\times 25 \\\\  & =0.036\\times 25 \\\\  & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3.6 \\%$ of $25$ is $0.9.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n3.6 \\% = \\dfrac{3.6}{100} = \\dfrac{3.6 \\times 10}{100 \\times 10} = \\dfrac{36}{1,000}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =3.6%\\times 25 \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{1,000}\\times 25 \\\\  & =\\frac{900}{1,000} \\\\  & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3.6 \\%$ of $25$ is $0.9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147483 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20feb2c2-bcec-5730-be40-da2f8e44be59" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Percentage Greater Than 100%"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19b8e503-c914-5f4f-a769-b4db7c1e899d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "98" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441625} {:answer/id #uuid "6a6f0a6c-99f1-5217-a418-e6002fbb440e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441636} {:answer/id #uuid "94a01aad-55f8-59ec-bb0a-59641755c57c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "94" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441643} {:answer/id #uuid "e260a7cf-d462-5f20-9ef9-e12bca10caa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441651} {:answer/id #uuid "ff4488c6-c8c6-5d04-9e6a-88bca4dc6f00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "92" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff4488c6-c8c6-5d04-9e6a-88bca4dc6f00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "92" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441657} :answer-field/id #uuid "428eb806-1017-5c82-866c-5cb029c7791a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e7f35be5-687e-57cd-bcc5-6295920b0ded" :question/math-academy-id "q-160842" :question/problem "What is $115%$ of $80?$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $80,$ and the percentage is $115%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n115%=115÷100=1.15\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =115%\\times 80 \\\\  & =1.15\\times 80 \\\\  & =92\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $115%$ of $80$ is $92.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n115%=\\frac{115}{100}=\\frac{115÷5}{100÷5}=\\frac{23}{20}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =115%\\times 80 \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{20}\\times 80 \\\\  & =23\\times \\frac{80}{20} \\\\  & =23\\times 4 \\\\  & =92\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $115%$ of $80$ is $92.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441683 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0025f8a6-40fc-544b-abc7-e9c283da8f33" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Decimal Percentage"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "222d960a-6b24-52cb-a7d5-6b9ae0042537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441626} {:answer/id #uuid "49815158-cf3c-5be2-bbf6-84c56f3c9324" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441631} {:answer/id #uuid "4af2add2-4118-5742-aa05-3f2a4eaf1c4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441632} {:answer/id #uuid "6f959ade-dcdc-51d1-a2b9-989b6e916e24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441641} {:answer/id #uuid "a6db3596-f288-520e-8011-17f3adc2e5f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49815158-cf3c-5be2-bbf6-84c56f3c9324" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441631} :answer-field/id #uuid "8de07806-3226-599c-87f5-c4c81b05f738" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6cea0e8-6d8a-5845-b043-a8160aa27bec" :question/math-academy-id "q-160849" :question/problem "What is $1.5%$ of $60?$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $60,$ and the percentage is $1.5%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n1.5%=1.5÷100=0.015\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =1.5%\\times 60 \\\\  & =0.015\\times 60 \\\\  & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $1.5%$ of $60$ is $0.9.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n1.5%=\\frac{1.5}{100}=\\frac{1.5\\times 10}{100\\times 10}=\\frac{15}{1,000}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =1.5%\\times 60 \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{1,000}\\times 60 \\\\  & =\\frac{900}{1,000} \\\\  & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $1.5%$ of $60$ is $0.9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441675 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0025f8a6-40fc-544b-abc7-e9c283da8f33" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Decimal Percentage"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39f57abf-84f0-5cf5-89fc-da5c8c9da016" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441629} {:answer/id #uuid "9087d490-4c3d-5031-987f-33fb68a2fb29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441642} {:answer/id #uuid "d1f5bfe7-fecb-54af-8e2a-3bad03ba48ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441649} {:answer/id #uuid "f5355f84-24dc-5530-87e1-1d90921a77df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441654} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe1bb64-8aae-508c-9666-6fd610795f95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9087d490-4c3d-5031-987f-33fb68a2fb29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441642} :answer-field/id #uuid "0495fce3-5e30-538c-9858-e374c612f1de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "41c7e58b-9463-581a-ad4d-8589209fcfa8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160856" :question/problem "What is $0.4%$ of $150?$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $150,$ and the percentage is $0.4%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n0.4%=0.4÷100=0.004\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.4%\\times 150 \\\\  & =0.004\\times 150 \\\\  & =0.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.4%$ of $150$ is $0.6.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n0.4%=\\frac{0.4}{100}=\\frac{0.4\\times 10}{100\\times 10}=\\frac{4}{1,000}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.4%\\times 150 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{1,000}\\times 150 \\\\  & =\\frac{600}{1,000} \\\\  & =0.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.4%$ of $150$ is $0.6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441680 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0025f8a6-40fc-544b-abc7-e9c283da8f33" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Decimal Percentage"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c239089-9b3b-5b6e-9a2a-29cb0f5b6d5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441637} {:answer/id #uuid "a57a33d2-a0d9-542c-88ae-e5612d73beb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441644} {:answer/id #uuid "d157906d-c910-5bc1-8716-5b2bd5c9c021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441648} {:answer/id #uuid "db71a8a8-0d3a-5054-8025-613a094f0cd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441650} {:answer/id #uuid "fa0036d8-b66f-5a31-96bb-ab88630d96e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c239089-9b3b-5b6e-9a2a-29cb0f5b6d5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441637} :answer-field/id #uuid "86b60ba2-2790-559a-9637-46791c78910f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91d7c0f9-d7dc-529a-84d9-52cae01b410f" :question/math-academy-id "q-160859" :question/problem "What is $0.25%$ of $400?$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $400,$ and the percentage is $0.25%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n0.25%=0.25÷100=0.0025\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.25%\\times 400 \\\\  & =0.0025\\times 400 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.25%$ of $400$ is $1.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n0.25%=\\frac{0.25}{100}=\\frac{0.25\\times 100}{100\\times 100}=\\frac{25}{10,000}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.25%\\times 400 \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{10,000}\\times 400 \\\\  & =\\frac{10,000}{10,000} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.25%$ of $400$ is $1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441674 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0025f8a6-40fc-544b-abc7-e9c283da8f33" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Decimal Percentage"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce900006-c571-5d1a-8205-026be13ff645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce900006-c571-5d1a-8205-026be13ff645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441647} :answer-field/id #uuid "16a584d9-8da8-58a7-8608-91d1146e977f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "338475e3-69eb-591d-aac8-e4880e67ce0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-171151" :question/problem "$0.4%$ of $750$ is equal to{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $750,$ and the percentage is $0.4%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n0.4%=0.4÷100=0.004\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.4%\\times 750 \\\\  & =0.004\\times 750 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.4%$ of $750$ is $3.$ \n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n0.4%=\\frac{0.4}{100}=\\frac{0.4\\times 10}{100\\times 10}=\\frac{4}{1,000}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.4%\\times 750 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{1,000}\\times 750 \\\\  & =\\frac{3,000}{1,000} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.4%$ of $750$ is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441676 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147482 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0e1c05a-7c23-59f5-a549-ec9a8d0415e6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Percentage"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60147acb